# f1 = make, f2 = area, f3 = count, f4 = areaOfText, f5 = measure
# `measure` has a guard on `box`, and so a slow body. `area` goes by what its callers leave, and Link proves nothing of `made`: `areaOfText` hands over what only its own test tells.
# The records of a slow body say nothing of positions: that of `make(...sizes)` says `anything`. What the walk leaves at `area` is what the one function that is called hands back
# (Walker::typeThatCallByValueIsShownToGive()), and the judge of calls asks the same rule. `f2:0:L0` says what the unit of the text has left at entry parameter 0 of f2.
# RUN: verify-code f2:0:L0 f2:1:i32 mechanisms=all
# CHECK: verified
# -- code
# code f5:SlowBody {
#   v0: 2 @Int32 = Integer integer=2
#   b0(v1: anything?ParameterOfEscapedFunction @JSValue, v2: anything?ParameterOfEscapedFunction @JSValue) entry=0:
#     v3: Array @Cell = NewArray contents=anything traits=[mayCollect, mayTouchMemory]
#     v4: f1 @JSValue = GetModuleVariable variable=g0 traits=[mayCollect, mayTouchMemory]
#     v5: anything?ResultOfUnknownCallee @JSValue = CallList v4, -, v3 traits=[mayThrow, mayThrowByRule, mayCollect, mayCallUnknownCode, mayBeTerminated, mayWriteWhatIsSeen, mayTouchMemory, mayWriteOutsideObjects]
#     v6: i32 @Int32 = CallDirect v5, v0 function=f2 traits=[mayThrow, mayThrowByRule, mayCollect, mayCallUnknownCode, mayBeTerminated, mayWriteWhatIsSeen, mayTouchMemory, mayWriteOutsideObjects]
#     v7: i32 @JSValue = Box v6
#     v8: i32 @Double = Unbox v7
#     Return v8
# }
# -- end of code
